Permaculture·Pioneer plants · Annuals · Perennials · Succession · Companion planting
Permaculture # a design approach based on understandings of how nature works! includes a set of principles derived using whole-systems thinking.
Pioneer plants # In less managed spaces, pioneer species/ plants are resilient species that are the first to colonize barren environments. In human-managed ecological restoration, pioneer plants can be used to restore soil qualities for more demanding plants.
Annuals # An annual plant is a plant that completes its life cycle – from germination to the production of seeds – within one growing season, and then dies.
Perennials # Perennial is used to differentiate a plant from shorter-lived annuals and biennials. It has thus been defined as a plant that lives more than 2 years.
